## Why GeoJSON is the right choice for ~50 US locations

| Metric | Typical value for your case | What it means for MapLibre |
|--------|----------------------------|----------------------------|
| **Feature count** | 50 | Well under the “sweet-spot” < 5 000-feature guideline. |
| **File size** | < 100 KB (even with properties) | Loads in a few milliseconds on any connection; parsing time is negligible. |
| **Update frequency** | Likely occasional (add/remove stores) | You can just replace the GeoJSON file or edit the inline object – no tile rebuild needed. |
| **Interactivity** | Click/hover for details, maybe clustering | GeoJSON gives you full client-side access to every feature’s properties, so you can attach `click` listeners, filter, cluster, etc., without extra server work. |
| **Zoom-dependent styling** | Not required (stores are points) | You can style the points once; no need for multiple zoom-levels of detail. |

The **GeoJSON performance thresholds** in the skill state:

| Range | Size / features | Behaviour |
|-------|----------------|-----------|
| Sweet spot | < 2 MB / < 5 000 features | Instant load, smooth interaction |
| Lag zone | 5–20 MB / up to ~50 000 features | 1–3 s parse delay, mobile may struggle |
| Crash zone | > 50 MB / > 100 000 features | Browser freeze or crash – switch to tiles |

Your dataset sits comfortably in the *sweet spot*.

