## How to add the store locations

### 1. Put the data somewhere the browser can fetch it

*Option A – static file* (`stores.geojson` in your web root)

```json
{
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "features": [
    {
      "type": "Feature",
      "properties": { "name": "Store A", "address": "123 Main St, Anytown, NY" },
      "geometry": { "type": "Point", "coordinates": [-73.9857, 40.7484] }
    }
    // … 49 more features …
  ]
}
```

*Option B – inline data* (useful for demos or when the file is tiny)

```js
const storesGeoJSON = {
  type: "FeatureCollection",
  features: [
    { type: "Feature", properties: { name: "Store A" }, geometry: { type: "Point", coordinates: [-73.9857, 40.7484] } },
    // …
  ]
};
```

### 2. Add the source and a layer in MapLibre GL JS

```javascript
// Assuming you already have a MapLibre map instance called `map`
map.addSource('stores', {
  type: 'geojson',
  // Use either a URL or the inline object
  data: '/stores.geojson'          // <-- Option A
  // data: storesGeoJSON           // <-- Option B
});

map.addLayer({
  id: 'store-points',
  type: 'circle',                 // or 'symbol' if you want icons/labels
  source: 'stores',
  paint: {
    'circle-radius': 6,
    'circle-color': '#ff6600',
    'circle-stroke-width': 1,
    'circle-stroke-color': '#fff'
  }
});
```

### 3. Add interactivity (click, hover, pop-ups)

```javascript
map.on('click', 'store-points', (e) => {
  const props = e.features[0].properties;
  new maplibregl.Popup()
    .setLngLat(e.lngLat)
    .setHTML(`<strong>${props.name}</strong><br>${props.address}`)
    .addTo(map);
});

// Optional: change cursor on hover
map.on('mouseenter', 'store-points', () => map.getCanvas().style.cursor = 'pointer');
map.on('mouseleave', 'store-points', () => map.getCanvas().style.cursor = '');
```

### 4. (Optional) Cluster the points for better UX at low zoom

```javascript
map.addSource('stores', {
  type: 'geojson',
  data: '/stores.geojson',
  cluster: true,
  clusterMaxZoom: 14, // max zoom to cluster points on
  clusterRadius: 50   // pixel radius of each cluster
});

map.addLayer({
  id: 'clusters',
  type: 'circle',
  source: 'stores',
  filter: ['has', 'point_count'],
  paint: {
    'circle-color': '#ff6600',
    'circle-radius': ['step', ['get', 'point_count'], 15, 10, 20, 30, 25]
  }
});

map.addLayer({
  id: 'cluster-count',
  type: 'symbol',
  source: 'stores',
  filter: ['has', 'point_count'],
  layout: {
    'text-field': '{point_count_abbreviated}',
    'text-font': ['Open Sans Bold', 'Arial Unicode MS Bold'],
    'text-size': 12
  }
});

map.addLayer({
  id: 'unclustered-point',
  type: 'circle',
  source: 'stores',
  filter: ['!', ['has', 'point_count']],
  paint: {
    'circle-color': '#ff6600',
    'circle-radius': 6,
    'circle-stroke-width': 1,
    'circle-stroke-color': '#fff'
  }
});
```

